# Building PartiuRolê from zero to scale

PartiuRolê is a full digital ticket marketplace I built from scratch and launched to production in just **6 months**. More than a single app, it is a complete commerce ecosystem for live events, designed to connect buyers and producers through a reliable, high-performance, and scalable product experience.

From day one, the objective was ambitious: deliver a real business-ready platform, not a prototype. That meant building fast without sacrificing architecture quality, developer velocity, or long-term scalability. The stack was chosen to maximize performance and productivity: **Bun** and **Elysia** on the backend, **Next.js** for web experiences, and **React Native** for mobile.

## A marketplace built as a four-platform product

One of the most strategic decisions was to architect PartiuRolê as **four dedicated platforms**, each optimized for a distinct user journey:

- **Buyer Web App**: discovery, checkout, and ticket management.
- **Producer Web App**: event creation, pricing, ticket batches, and sales operations.
- **Buyer Mobile App**: a fast, on-the-go purchase experience with ticket access in seconds.
- **Producer Mobile App**: mobile-first operational control for event teams and organizers.

Instead of forcing all roles into a single interface, each platform was intentionally designed for clarity, speed, and conversion. This separation dramatically improved usability while reducing friction in critical flows like event publishing, purchase completion, and post-sale operations.

## Engineering choices that accelerated delivery

Choosing **Bun + Elysia** gave us a lean and modern backend foundation with excellent runtime performance and a developer experience focused on velocity. On the frontend, **Next.js** enabled robust SEO-friendly pages and business-critical web flows, while **React Native** delivered native-feeling mobile apps with strong code reuse potential and predictable iteration speed.

This architecture made it possible to:

- move quickly across multiple products without losing consistency;
- establish reusable domain patterns for authentication, payments, and ticket lifecycle;
- keep development modular, so each platform could evolve independently;
- support growth with clear service boundaries and cloud-native deployment.

## AI as a force multiplier, not a shortcut

A major differentiator in this project was how AI was used as an integrated engineering capability across the full lifecycle. It was not treated as a gimmick or a code generator in isolation. Instead, AI acted as a **force multiplier** for decision-making, implementation speed, and quality assurance.

We used AI to accelerate:

- architecture exploration and technical trade-off analysis;
- rapid prototyping of complex user flows;
- generation and refinement of repetitive yet critical implementation patterns;
- code review support and edge-case thinking;
- documentation and knowledge sharing across product domains.

This AI-assisted workflow allowed us to compress the timeline from idea to production without compromising technical standards. The result was a practical blend of craftsmanship and velocity: faster cycles, better consistency, and higher confidence during releases.

## Shipping in 6 months with production-grade standards

Going from zero to production in half a year required tight execution across engineering, product, and infrastructure. We prioritized battle-tested foundations early: observability, deployment automation, environment management, and resilient cloud architecture. By investing in these capabilities from the beginning, we avoided common scaling bottlenecks later.

The platform was fully deployed on **AWS**, with an end-to-end cloud strategy designed for reliability and elasticity. Infrastructure decisions focused on predictable operations, safer rollout flows, and room for growth as user volume and event complexity increase.

## Business impact through technical excellence

PartiuRolê demonstrates what happens when modern architecture, focused product thinking, and AI-accelerated execution come together under strong engineering discipline. It is a showcase of building a marketplace that is not only functional, but also operationally mature and ready to scale.

For me as a developer, this project represents more than a delivery milestone. It reflects a way of building products where speed and quality reinforce each other: clear architecture, role-specific experiences, smart automation, and a cloud-native backbone that supports real market growth.

PartiuRolê is the proof: a digital ticket marketplace built from zero, launched in 6 months, structured across four platforms, and engineered for scale on AWS.
